cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Sharjah Criterion: A Two-Stage Empirical Lunar Crescent Visibility Model"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-06-19"
authors:
  - family-names: Talafha
    given-names: Mohammed
    email: mtalafha901@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtalafha90/Sharjah_Criterion"
abstract: >
  A data-driven two-stage logistic-regression criterion for lunar crescent
  visibility, derived from ICOP crescent sighting reports. The pipeline
  scrapes, cleans, and enriches observations with astronomical features,
  trains stage-1 (detectability) and stage-2 (naked-eye vs. aided) models,
  selects operational thresholds, and validates externally against the
  Alrefay et al. (2018) published tables.
keywords:
  - lunar crescent
  - crescent visibility
  - Islamic calendar
  - hilal
  - logistic regression
  - astronomical criterion
  - ICOP
  - Alrefay
license: MIT
